                <pb facs="1420" n="1304" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg1304"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 6.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Morgenthau to the Minister for Foreign
                        Affairs</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-06-03">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 3, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">note verbale.</hi>
                </p>
                <p>The Embassy of the United States of America has had the honor to receive the note
                    verbale of the Imperial Ministry dated May 31, 1915, No. 66421/107, in regard to
                    the intervention of American consular officers in matters which concern their
                    nationals in the Ottoman Empire.</p>
                <p>In reply, this Embassy has the honor to again refer to its notes of September 18,
                    1914, and of May 7, 1915, No. 285.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
